{
  "title": "TuShare \u2014 fintech (15,018\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: TuShare\nDomain: fintech | Scale: medium | Stars: 15,018\nProblem: TuShare provides a utility for crawling, cleaning, and storing historical financial data (stocks, futures) from Chinese markets. It simplifies data acquisition for quantitative analysts and data enthusiasts.\nTarget users: Quantitative finance analysts, Data science learners, Chinese stock market traders, Financial research professionals\nCore features: Historical stock price data retrieval (OHLCV with moving averages); Real-time and daily trading data for all listed stocks; Tick-level transaction history data; Adjusted price data (forward and backward adjustment); Date range filtering and customizable time periods; Pandas DataFrame output format for easy analysis\nIntegrations: Chinese stock exchange data sources, Tushare Pro API (paid tier)\nTech stack: Python\nKey libraries: pandas, requests, lxml, beautifulsoup4, simplejson\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Data-centric design: Library focuses on ETL operations (extraction, transformation, load) rather than building a full application stack, returning processed pandas DataFrames for downstream analysis\n- Web scraping approach: Uses BeautifulSoup and lxml for HTML parsing, suggesting data is aggregated from multiple Chinese financial websites rather than a single API\n- Simple abstraction: High-level functions (get_hist_data, get_today_all, get_tick_data) hide complexity, enabling non-specialists to access financial data via intuitive calls\n- Community-driven evolution: Migration to 'Tushare Pro' paid model indicates shift toward sustainable business model while maintaining core open-source library",
